<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute lateral sprain of the right ankle (S93.401A)</content>. Inversion sprain of the lateral ligaments. The Ottawa ankle rules are negative (no bony tenderness and able to bear weight), so no X-ray is needed. He takes duloxetine: tramadol is avoided because with duloxetine it can cause serotonin toxicity and seizures, and an oral NSAID is avoided because with an SNRI it raises the risk of stomach bleeding, so a topical NSAID is the better choice. [S]<list><item>A lace-up ankle brace and walking as pain allows; avoid long rest.</item><item>Ice for 15 minutes several times a day and elevation for the first few days.</item><item>Diclofenac 1% gel four times a day for up to two weeks, and acetaminophen up to 1 g three times a day.</item><item>No tramadol, and no other medicine for pain without checking, because of the duloxetine.</item><item>Balance and strengthening exercises from next week to prevent a repeat sprain.</item><item>Return for inability to walk, numbness, or a cold or pale foot.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-frostbite neuropathic pain of the fingers (M79.2)</content>. Stable on duloxetine. [S]<list><item>Continue duloxetine 60 mg daily.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Neuropathic pain in adults: pharmacological management in non-specialist settings (CG173) (2013, updated 2020); Diagnosis, treatment and prevention of ankle sprains: update of an evidence-based clinical guideline (Vuurberg G, et al. Br J Sports Med 2018;52(15):956) (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Telephone check in one week. Scheduled review in three weeks. Next scheduled visit 1928-06-09: seventeen-week review: finger pain, the ankle sprain, and the risks of an Arctic air search flight. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
